###> IDE ###
# Ignore the directory's contents, not the directory: Git never descends into an
# excluded directory, so a `!` negation inside one has no effect.
/.vscode/*
# Shared, not personal: settings.json wires format-on-save to the project's own
# php-cs-fixer, and it does nothing unless the recommended extension is
# installed — so both have to reach every clone.
!/.vscode/settings.json
!/.vscode/extensions.json
/.idea/
###< IDE ###

###> test output ###
/test_output.txt
###< test output ###

###> stray Windows temp-path dirs (e.g. a tool writing to "C:\..." as a relative path) ###
/[A-Za-z]:/
